Use io and list.

Define function search_rotated taking nums as a pointer to List of whole number, target as a whole number returning a whole number:
    Let n be count of nums.
    Let low start at 0 as a whole number.
    Let high be n as a whole number - 1.
    Repeat while low is at most high:
        Let middle be low + (high - low) divided by 2.
        Let value be list_get(nums, middle as an unsigned number).
        If value equals target:
            Give back middle.
        Let low value be list_get(nums, low as an unsigned number).
        If low value is at most value:
            If target is at least low value and target is less than value:
                Set high to middle - 1.
            Otherwise:
                Set low to middle + 1.
        Otherwise:
            Let high value be list_get(nums, high as an unsigned number).
            If target is more than value and target is at most high value:
                Set low to middle + 1.
            Otherwise:
                Set high to middle - 1.
    Give back -1.
Done.

Let nums be a list of 4, 5, 6, 7, 0, 1, and 2.
Say search_rotated(address of nums, 0).
Say search_rotated(address of nums, 3).
list_free(address of nums).
Return 0.
